; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Polygon Parade
; CATEGORY: Shapes & Polygons
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     polygon, total turtle trip, labels, lists
; SUMMARY:  Draws every regular polygon from 3 to 10 sides, each with its name underneath.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Eight shapes march across the screen in two rows: triangle,
;   square, pentagon, hexagon, heptagon, octagon, nonagon and
;   decagon. Every shape is drawn by the same little procedure.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Then try  poly 12 30  or  poly 20 15  yourself.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * the Total Turtle Trip: the turns of any closed shape add up to 360
;   * so each turn of a regular polygon is 360 / sides
;   * keeping names in a list and picking one out with ITEM
;   * LABEL writes words in the turtle world
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * What happens with  poly 36 10 ? And  poly 360 1 ?
;   * Add "hendecagon to the list and draw 11 sides too.
;   * Make the side shorter when there are more sides so all
;     the shapes are about the same width.
; ============================================================

; One procedure for every regular polygon. The turtle makes
; :sides equal turns that together add up to one full turn.
to poly :sides :length
  repeat :sides [forward :length right 360 / :sides]
end

; Names for 3 sides, 4 sides, ... 10 sides.
make "names [triangle square pentagon hexagon heptagon octagon nonagon decagon]

; Draw the polygon with n sides centred over the spot (x, y)
; and write its name under it. To keep the shapes about the
; same size, a side gets shorter when there are more sides.
to showpolygon :n :x :y
  localmake "side 330 / :n
  penup
  setxy :x - :side / 2 :y
  setheading 90
  pendown
  setpencolor item :n - 2 [1 4 2 13 14 5 10 8]
  ; heading 90 means the first side runs along the bottom,
  ; and turning LEFT makes the shape go up instead of down
  repeat :n [forward :side left 360 / :n]
  penup
  setxy :x - 30 :y - 30
  setpencolor 0
  label item :n - 2 :names
end

clearscreen setlabelheight 16
setpensize 3

; top row: 3, 4, 5, 6 sides
for [n 3 6] [showpolygon :n -270 + 180 * (:n - 3) 60]
; bottom row: 7, 8, 9, 10 sides
for [n 7 10] [showpolygon :n -270 + 180 * (:n - 7) -200]

penup setxy -150 250 setpencolor 1 setlabelheight 20
label [Every shape turns 360 degrees in all]
hideturtle
